    <span class="ngo-eyebrow">Common questions</span>
    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <details><summary><h3>What is the Social Stock Exchange for NGOs?</h3><span class="ngo-faq-icon">+</span></summary><p>The SSE is a SEBI-regulated marketplace where registered non-profit organisations raise funds through Zero Coupon Zero Principal (ZCZP) instruments — non-repayable, grant-like securities with structured impact reporting obligations.</p></details>
    <details><summary><h3>What is a ZCZP instrument and how does it work?</h3><span class="ngo-faq-icon">+</span></summary><p>A ZCZP instrument is a SEBI-regulated security through which NGOs raise funds without any obligation to repay principal or interest. The NGO commits to structured impact measurement and reporting submitted to SEBI.</p></details>
    <details><summary><h3>How long does the SSE readiness process take?</h3><span class="ngo-faq-icon">+</span></summary><p>Typically 6 to 12 weeks, depending on your NGO's current governance, documentation and compliance maturity. Our Phase 1 Diagnostic gives a clear, personalised timeline within the first two weeks.</p></details>
    <details><summary><h3>Can smaller NGOs participate in the Social Stock Exchange?</h3><span class="ngo-faq-icon">+</span></summary><p>Yes — provided the NGO meets SEBI eligibility criteria and can demonstrate measurable social impact. We have supported NGOs with fundraising targets starting from ₹50 lakhs.</p></details>
    <details><summary><h3>Does listing on the SSE guarantee fundraising success?</h3><span class="ngo-faq-icon">+</span></summary><p>No. SSE listing creates access, not guaranteed outcomes. Success depends on governance credibility, the strength of your ZCZP case and how well your NGO is positioned for impact investing engagement.</p></details>
    <details><summary><h3>Is DR Associates SEBI-registered or affiliated?</h3><span class="ngo-faq-icon">+</span></summary><p>DR Associates operates as a specialised SSE consultancy working within SEBI's regulatory framework. For official guidelines, refer to sebi.gov.in.</p></details>
